  "timelapse": 8,
  "steps": [
    {
      "say": "Here is an analog wristwatch, the kind with hands that sweep around a circle. Let's take it apart and see how it tells the time!",
      "do": [
        {
          "reveal": [
            "case",
            "movement",
            "dial",
            "hand_post",
            "hour_hand",
            "minute_hand",
            "second_hand",
            "crystal",
            "crown",
            "strap_top",
            "strap_bottom"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "all"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "Look at the three hands. The short one is the hour hand, the long one is the minute hand, and the thin red one is the second hand. They all sit on one little center post, stacked like pancakes.",
      "do": [
        {
          "explode": "all"
        },
        {
          "label": [
            "hour_hand",
            "minute_hand",
            "second_hand",
            "hand_post"
          ]
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "hour_hand",
            "minute_hand",
            "second_hand"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "hand_post"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "Each hand moves at its own speed. The second hand goes all the way around in one minute. The minute hand takes a whole hour. The hour hand is the slowpoke: it goes around twice a day. We've sped them up so you can watch.",
      "do": [
        {
          "spin": [
            "hour_hand",
            "minute_hand",
            "second_hand"
          ]
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "second_hand"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "The dial is the face. Its marks split the circle into twelve hours, like slices of a pizza. Where the short hand points tells the hour, and the long hand tells the minutes.",
      "do": [
        {
          "label": [
            "dial"
          ]
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "dial"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "dial"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "Hidden under the dial is the movement, the watch's engine. A wound-up spring or a tiny battery gives it power, and its gears pass the turning along, slowing it down from one hand to the next, like bicycle gears.",
      "do": [
        {
          "label": [
            "movement"
          ]
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "movement"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "movement"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "The metal case holds everything safely, and the clear crystal on top keeps dust and fingers off the hands. The little knob on the side is the crown: you pull and turn it to set the right time. The straps hold it on your wrist.",
      "do": [
        {
          "label": [
            "case",
            "crystal",
            "crown",
            "strap_top",
            "strap_bottom"
          ]
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "crown"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "case"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "Now let's put it all back together. Power turns the gears, the gears turn the hands at just the right speeds, and the dial tells you what time it is!",
      "do": [
        {
          "explode": []
        },
        {
          "zoom": "all"
        },
        {
          "spin": [
            "hour_hand",
            "minute_hand",
            "second_hand"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "recap": "Inside a watch, gears turn three hands at different speeds, so the second, minute and hour hands point to the time on the dial.",
  "question": "Would you like to find out how the tiny gears inside know exactly how fast to turn?",
  "layout": {
    "template": "blueprint",
    "explode": "free"
  }
}